Ahead of the new Mac Studio with M5 Max and M5 Ultra chips <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/new-mac-mini-and-mac-studio-launch-tomorrow/">launching this Tuesday</a>, the first reviews of the computer have been shared by selected tech websites and YouTube channels. According to one review <a href="https://www.macworld.com/article/3238319/mac-studio-m5-max-review.html">published by <em>Macworld</em>'s Roman Loyola</a>, the biggest upgrade isn't even the M5 Ultra, but rather significantly faster storage speeds.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/06/Mac-Studio-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1005928" /><br/>
"Typically, we start our reviews by looking at overall performance with Geekbench, and then we work our way through more specific aspects," he said. "But the SSD performance is so overwhelmingly good, it's the story here."<br/>
<br/>
Loyola ran Blackmagic's Disk Speed Test benchmark tool on the new Mac Studio with an 18-core M5 Max chip, 128GB of RAM, and a 4TB SSD, and the computer achieved around 2.6× faster SSD read speeds and around 2.1× faster SSD write speeds compared to a previous-generation Mac Studio with the M4 Max chip. The results are shown in the image below.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Mac-Studio-M5-Max-Blackmagic.jpeg" alt="" width="1200" height="850" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066416" /><br/>
Indeed, Apple advertised up to 2× faster storage speeds for the new Mac Studio, and these benchmark results show an even bigger boost. As always, real-world performance may vary, but expect significantly faster SSD speeds overall.<br/>
<br/>
M5 Ultra benchmark results <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/15/apple-m5-ultra-chip-benchmark/">already surfaced last week</a> if you are interested in that.<br/>
<br/>
Unsurprisingly, the M5 Ultra is Apple's fastest chip ever. Based on Geekbench 7 results so far, it has up to around 30% faster single-core CPU performance and up to around 35% faster multi-core performance compared to the M3 Ultra.<br/>
<br/>
Apple said the M5 Ultra has up to 1.25× faster single-threaded CPU performance and up to 1.3× faster multi-threaded CPU performance compared to the M3 Ultra, so the benchmark results roughly align with or even beat those advertised claims.<br/>
<br/>
All in all, the new Mac Studio is super fast, with <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/998040/apple-mac-studio-m5-ultra-initial-impressions-testing-review"><em>The Verge</em>'s Antonio G. Di Benedetto</a> describing the M5 Ultra model's performance as "outrageous" and <a href="https://ca.pcmag.com/desktop-pcs/18183/apple-mac-studio-2026-m5-ultra-review-quad-die-processing-power-to-die-for"><em>PCMag</em>'s Brian Westover</a> calling the computer "a serious powerhouse for top-tier local AI inference."<br/>
<br/>
The new Mac Studio and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-announces-2026-mac-mini/">a new Mac mini</a> with M6 and M5 Pro chip options have been available to pre-order since August 25 and launch this Tuesday, September 22.<br/>
<br/>
